module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.ProperCohomologyFiniteness

/-!
# Tag 0897 part (1) with the affine finite-type predicate

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum` states
[Stacks, Tag 0897] part (1) with finite type of the graded module `F` read as the sectionwise
`SheafOfModules.GradedModule.IsFiniteType`. This file states the same implication with finite
type read as the affine `Stacks.Coherent.IsFiniteTypeOnAffine`, which is the predicate the
Rees-algebra chain of [Stacks, Tag 02O8] can supply (through
`Stacks.Blowup.isFiniteTypeOnAffine_reesGradedModule`) and the one part (2),
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.exists_isZero_pieceTwistCohomology`, is stated
with.

## Main results

* `moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum_of_tag02O6` — part (1) with the affine predicate, granted the
  base change and [Stacks, Tag 02O6] as the hypothesis `Tag02O6`.
* `moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum'` — the same with `Tag02O6` discharged by `tag02O6`.

## Implementation notes

**The two statements of part (1) differ in the finite-type hypothesis and in nothing else.**
`SheafOfModules.GradedModule.IsFiniteType` asks for generation by finitely many homogeneous
sections on the members of *some* covering family of the site;
`Stacks.Coherent.IsFiniteTypeOnAffine` asks that the sections over *every* affine open be
generated by one finite family, with no covering and no localisation. Neither implies the other,
and no lemma in this library connects them. Since the hypothesis is inert in this implication —
finite type of `F` enters the source's argument only in producing `F'` and its coherence, which
are binders here — both forms are stated, and neither weakens the other.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached here: Tag 0897 has its site on
`moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum_and_exists_isZero_pieceTwistCohomology`, and these are forms of
its part (1).
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0897] part (1) with the affine finite-type predicate, granted
[Stacks, Tag 02O6] and the base change.** Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `B` a finitely generated
graded `A`-algebra, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` proper and `F` a quasi-coherent graded `𝓑`-module of finite
type. Then the graded `B`-module `⨁ₙ H^p(X, Fₙ)` is a finite `B`-module, for every `p`.

The hypotheses beyond the source's are the base change of the source's proof —
`f' : X' ⟶ Spec B` proper with a coherent `F'` on `X'`, the graded `B`-action on
`⨁ₙ H^p(X, Fₙ)`, and the `B`-linear comparison `cmp` with `H^p(X', F')` that
[Stacks, Tag 089W] provides because `X' ⟶ X` is affine — together with `Tag02O6`.

Given those, [Stacks, Tag 02O6] applies to `f'` with the ring `B`: `B` is Noetherian because it
is a finitely generated algebra over the Noetherian ring `A`, and `F'` is coherent, so
`H^p(X', F')` is a finite `B`-module and `cmp` carries that finiteness back to
`⨁ₙ H^p(X, Fₙ)`. -/
theorem moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum_of_tag02O6 {X : Scheme.{u}}
    {𝓑 : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} X.ringCatSheaf}
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule A B) [_root_.GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [Algebra.FiniteType A B]
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) [IsProper f]
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedModule 𝓑)
    (_hqc : ∀ n : ℤ, (pieceModule F n).IsQuasicoherent)
    (_hft : Stacks.Coherent.IsFiniteTypeOnAffine F)
    (h02O6 : Tag02O6.{u}) (p : ℕ)
    {X' : Scheme.{u}} (f' : X' ⟶ Spec (.of B)) [IsProper f']
    (F' : X'.Modules) [F'.IsCoherent]
    [Module B (gradedCohomologySum F p)]
    (cmp : gradedCohomologySum F p ≃ₗ[B]
      ↥((ModuleCat.restrictScalars (specAlgebraRingHom B f')).obj
        (cohomologyOf X' p F'))) :
    Module.Finite B (gradedCohomologySum F p) :=
  have hBN : IsNoetherianRing B := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing A B
  have _hfin : Module.Finite B
      ↥((ModuleCat.restrictScalars (specAlgebraRingHom B f')).obj (cohomologyOf X' p F')) :=
    h02O6 B hBN X' f' inferInstance F' inferInstance p
  Module.Finite.equiv cmp.symm

/-- **Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0897] with the affine finite-type predicate, and with no
[Stacks, Tag 02O6] hypothesis.** Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `B` a finitely generated graded
`A`-algebra, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` proper and `F` a quasi-coherent graded `𝓑`-module of finite type.
Granted the base change of the source's proof, the graded `B`-module `⨁ₙ H^p(X, Fₙ)` is a finite
`B`-module for every `p`.

This is `moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum_of_tag02O6` with its hypothesis `h02O6` discharged by
`tag02O6`. It differs from `moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum` in the finite-type predicate alone;
the Rees-algebra chain of [Stacks, Tag 02O8] consumes this one, because
`Stacks.Blowup.isFiniteTypeOnAffine_reesGradedModule` is what it can supply. -/
theorem moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum' {X : Scheme.{u}}
    {𝓑 : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} X.ringCatSheaf}
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule A B) [_root_.GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [Algebra.FiniteType A B]
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) [IsProper f]
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedModule 𝓑)
    (hqc : ∀ n : ℤ, (pieceModule F n).IsQuasicoherent)
    (hft : Stacks.Coherent.IsFiniteTypeOnAffine F)
    (p : ℕ)
    {X' : Scheme.{u}} (f' : X' ⟶ Spec (.of B)) [IsProper f']
    (F' : X'.Modules) [F'.IsCoherent]
    [Module B (gradedCohomologySum F p)]
    (cmp : gradedCohomologySum F p ≃ₗ[B]
      ↥((ModuleCat.restrictScalars (specAlgebraRingHom B f')).obj
        (cohomologyOf X' p F'))) :
    Module.Finite B (gradedCohomologySum F p) :=
  moduleFinite_gradedCohomologySum_of_tag02O6 A 𝒜 f F hqc hft tag02O6.{u} p f' F' cmp

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology

end
